      "priority": "P2",
      "id": "r7-deployment-001",
      "file": "deploy/safe_fs.py",
      "line": 131,
      "trigger": "An untrusted build produces a very wide directory before it exits. Builder.prepare then calls privileged snapshot(build/app, export/app) at deploy/build.py:281 after the producer stops. snapshot first evaluates sorted(os.listdir(fd)), before checking MAX_FILES at line134; inspect_tree likewise lets os.walk materialize a whole directory before line199 enforces its count.",
      "impact": "The advertised150000-entry cap does not bound privileged enumeration memory or sorting work. Candidate-created names, including hardlink names that would later be rejected, are all allocated first; candidate stage memory limits no longer contain this allocation. A sufficiently wide output can exhaust the importer/host resources before the intended budget error. This is an import resource-boundary flaw, not evidence of path escape or arbitrary root execution.",
      "evidence": [
        "Fresh Windows actual inspect_tree witness with2000 empty files and MAX_FILES temporarily3 consumed all2000 DirEntries before Tree file budget exceeded.",
        "Fresh Linux actual fd snapshot witness under nobody UID65534: os.listdir received a real directory descriptor and returned2000 names; only3 entries were copied before Tree has too many files. No huge directory or OOM was attempted.",
