    {
      "priority": "P2",
      "id": "r7-deployment-002",
      "file": "deploy/safe_fs.py",
      "line": 77,
      "trigger": "A source tar contains many ordinary file headers with distinct nested parent paths, omitting separate directory headers. extract_tar counts physical headers at lines63-64, but tree_mkdir(target.parent,destination) recursively creates all missing parents without charging them to a filesystem-entry budget.",
      "impact": "The tar member budget does not bound filesystem entries created during extraction. Builder.prepare extracts the untrusted archive directly into the ordinary stage/source at deploy/build.py:231-232 before its4/8GiB loop workspaces exist. Deep path prefixes can multiply disk/inode consumption on the privileged host filesystem; later inspect_tree rejection arrives only after those directories have already been created. Header/payload byte limits and per-file content limits do not charge these empty directory inodes.",
      "evidence": [
        "Fresh Windows actual extract_tar fixture with MAX_FILES temporarily3 and only2 one-byte file headers (first/a/b/c/file and second/a/b/c/file) returned successfully after creating10 filesystem entries. No links, special members, large directory or disk filling were required.",
        {
          "file": ".work/round7/r7-deployment-implicit-directories-repro.py",
          "sha256": "5f5c5449013aab2a953ba44156564eae05191fec7ca7220b8777a563b92ef49d"
        },
        {
          "file": ".work/round7/r7-deployment-implicit-directories-result.json",
          "sha256": "22b765d602d72fa8e1f83d61678b574a9ee6feef7e1f2964f8b9664cb66182d2"
        },
        "tree_mkdir uses parents=True at line28; extract_tar entries tracks only explicit members. Count each newly created implicit directory before creation in addition to physical tar-header limits; ensure root source preparation has an enforced storage budget."
      ]
    }
